I like Rupesh sir In C++, a constructor  is a special member function of a 
class that is automatically called whenever an object of the 
class is created. The primary role of a constructor is to 
initialize the object 
1. similar to member function 
2. has same name as class name 
3. called automatically when object of class created 
4. A constructor is used to initialize the objects of class as 
soon as the object is created. 


