Properties of Constructor 
▪Constructor  should be declared in public 
section because private constructor cannot be 
invoked outside the class so they are useless. 
▪Constructors do not have return types and 
they cannot return values, not even void. 
▪Constructors cannot be inherited, even though a derived class can call 
the base class constructor. 
▪Constructors cannot be virtual. class car
{
  private: 
    float  mileage; 
  public : 
    car() 
    { 
     cin>>mileage; 
    } 
};

