Copy Constructor 
▪A copy constructor is used to declare and initialize an object 
from another object using an object as argument. 
▪For example: 
   demo(demo &d);  //declaration 
        demo d2(d1);      //copy object 
OR   demo d2=d1;               //copy object 
▪Constructor which accepts a reference to its own class as a 
parameter is called copy constructor .

--- Page 25 ---
3/31/2025 Ms. Neeshu Chaudhary, CSE dept 25I like C++ so much 
I like Rupesh sir ▪A copy constructor is used to initialize an objec from another 
object using an object as argument. 
▪A Parameterized constructor which accepts a reference to its 
own class as a parameter is called copy constructor .

--- Page 26 ---
3/31/2025 Ms. Neeshu Chaudhary, CSE dept 26I like C++ so much 
I like Rupesh sir class demo 
{
   int m, n; 
   public :
   demo( int x,int y){
    m=x; 
    n=y; 
    cout<< "Parameterized Constructor" ;
   }
   demo(demo &x){ 
    m = x.m; 
    n = x.n; 
    cout<< "Copy Constructor" ;  
   } 
};int main() 
{ 
   demo obj1(5,6); 
   demo obj2(obj1); 
   demo obj2 = obj1;  
} 
5 6 m n obj1 
5 6 m n obj2 obj1 or x 

